  "id": "empf-v1",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "Raw mini-batch Sinkhorn couplings suffer from Poisson mode dropout and noisy batch-to-batch transport chords when K modes approach or exceed batch size B, while stranded prior particles can stall outside active critic basins. Inspired by e-means (arXiv:2611.09501), EMPF maintains a checkpointed online sufficient-statistics prototype bank (S, N) updated with clock-free (K, B) hit-rate EMA scaling and deterministic proportional-split dead-prototype revival, couples non-uniform prototype masses w_k = N_k / sum_j N_j to fake samples via entropic Optimal Transport, and pairs prototype-chord Born-Infeld critic bounding with an adaptive EMPF prior regularizer and outlier revival tether.",
